        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0529" n="427" xml:id="pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2126/53.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister
                    Furniss.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-01-22"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Root informs Mr. Furniss that it is understood the revolutionary leader at
                    St. Marc is at the American consulate, and also that there is evidence that he
                    is the agent of the conspirators in New York who are aiding the revolution. Mr.
                    Furniss is directed to inform the Haitian Government of the dismissal of the
                    consul and the cancellation of his commission. Instructs him to go or send a
                    responsible person to receive the archives.</p>
            </div>
